1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,336
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,339
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,341 --> 00:00:10,719
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,804
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:19,352
[Red] <i>Looks like Atoy struck the nerve</i>
<i>of other people too.</i>

7
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:21,938
<i>That's good.</i>
<i>That might make our job easier.</i>

8
00:00:22,021 --> 00:00:23,857
Just don't involve Gavin.

9
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:26,609
[Mongki] <i>It's not just those two</i>
<i>who were there, boss.</i>

10
00:00:26,693 --> 00:00:28,611
<i>Someone is protecting them.</i>

11
00:00:28,695 --> 00:00:30,238
Can we focus on the work?

12
00:00:30,321 --> 00:00:31,740
[Emerson] <i>Children of the thread.</i>

13
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:34,159
Tailor AFAM has arrived with his fam-bam.

14
00:00:34,242 --> 00:00:38,121
PREVIOUSLY

15
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:41,166
Damn it.

16
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:43,793
[Uno] There's another sleazebag.

17
00:00:43,877 --> 00:00:44,878
A sleazebag indeed.

18
00:00:44,961 --> 00:00:47,046
- [in English] You too! Eat!
- [mumbles]

19
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:48,840
[grunts]

20
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:52,927
[henchman] <i>Only Chiro</i>
<i>and the captives are with me,</i>

21
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:54,846
<i>so we can drink all night.</i>

22
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:57,515
We really need to get out of here
before more of them arrive.

23
00:00:57,599 --> 00:00:59,517
[Karla, in English] <i>Would you guys</i>
<i>like a private tour?</i>

24
00:00:59,601 --> 00:01:01,019
[in English] I would love to escort you.

25
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:02,896
- [in English] Let's go.
- [in English] Follow me.

26
00:01:02,979 --> 00:01:05,648
The child of Thread 2 is on the move.

27
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:07,317
Let's go, to the next location.

28
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:08,234
Hurry up.

29
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:09,986
Mini Thread is on the way.

30
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:12,113
[Charmi] Wow. It's beautiful.

31
00:01:12,197 --> 00:01:14,449
It's so beautiful here, Sister Faye.

32
00:01:14,532 --> 00:01:17,368
- I wish we could always come here.
- Ibyang!

33
00:01:17,952 --> 00:01:19,871
- [Ame] Ibyang!
- Sister Ame?!

34
00:01:20,872 --> 00:01:21,706
[both] Hey!

35
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:22,957
Oh.

36
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,546
[music fades]

37
00:01:32,967 --> 00:01:35,678
Sister, I miss you!

38
00:01:36,763 --> 00:01:38,264
I miss you more!

39
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:39,474
‪[light music playing]

40
00:01:39,557 --> 00:01:40,517
Wait.

41
00:01:41,017 --> 00:01:41,935
Why are you here?

42
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:43,311
What are you doing here, Faye?

43
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:47,315
Oh, we're meeting Olga here after her gig.

44
00:01:47,398 --> 00:01:49,109
[Ame] Ah!

45
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:54,697
And you, Sister Ame,
why are you alone here?

46
00:01:55,532 --> 00:01:58,284
Do you have someone
from Tabang Lupa with you?

47
00:01:59,452 --> 00:02:02,539
Yes. We have a mission. Shh.

48
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:03,998
Hey.

49
00:02:04,082 --> 00:02:06,417
Let me join!

50
00:02:06,501 --> 00:02:07,335
Not possible.

51
00:02:08,086 --> 00:02:09,796
This was already planned.

52
00:02:09,879 --> 00:02:11,464
- [Ibyang] Hmm.
- But fine.

53
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:13,258
Just say hi to Emerson, okay?

54
00:02:13,341 --> 00:02:14,175
- Okay.
- Faye.

55
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:18,096
- Hmm?
- What time will Olga be coming?

56
00:02:18,179 --> 00:02:19,264
[Charmi] Oh.

57
00:02:19,347 --> 00:02:20,807
Later tonight.

58
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:23,852
Uh, can I take Ibyang with me first?

59
00:02:23,935 --> 00:02:26,938
Just so she can say hi to our friends.

60
00:02:27,021 --> 00:02:29,983
They haven't seen her in a long time.

61
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:31,901
- You should come too.
- Oh.

62
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:33,778
- Huh?
- Okay, okay.

63
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:36,698
I'll text Olga so she can join us.

64
00:02:36,781 --> 00:02:37,615
Okay, let's go. Come on.

65
00:02:42,954 --> 00:02:44,789
[indistinct chattering]

66
00:02:45,623 --> 00:02:47,041
[suave theme music playing]

67
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:48,960
[motorcycle revving]

68
00:02:49,043 --> 00:02:49,919
[sewing machine whirring]

69
00:02:50,003 --> 00:02:50,879
[scratches]

70
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:52,881
[snipping]

71
00:02:52,964 --> 00:02:56,759
[sewing machine clacking]

72
00:02:56,843 --> 00:02:58,011
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

73
00:02:58,094 --> 00:03:00,138
[gunshots]

74
00:03:00,221 --> 00:03:02,432
[clicking]

75
00:03:02,515 --> 00:03:04,517
[snipping]

76
00:03:04,601 --> 00:03:05,560
[music swells]

77
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:10,148
[electronic blipping]

78
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:16,446
[ominous music playing]

79
00:03:16,529 --> 00:03:18,072
Son of a thread.

80
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:20,116
They really don't want
to let us out of here.

81
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:23,453
- [gate lock rattling]
- [Atoy sniffs]

82
00:03:30,251 --> 00:03:33,171
It's not working. It's not working.

83
00:03:33,254 --> 00:03:36,007
[Lily gasps]

84
00:03:36,674 --> 00:03:37,967
Nothing, nothing, nothing.

85
00:03:38,551 --> 00:03:40,678
Atoy, let's go around.
Maybe there's another gate open.

86
00:03:41,262 --> 00:03:43,806
If there's another gate,
it's surely locked too.

87
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:45,683
What do we do?

88
00:03:45,767 --> 00:03:47,018
[music fades]

89
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:49,479
If there's a lock,
that means there's a key.

90
00:03:49,562 --> 00:03:52,899
[suspicious music playing]

91
00:03:52,982 --> 00:03:53,858
I know.

92
00:03:54,525 --> 00:03:56,945
That place we passed earlier,
that was an office.

93
00:03:57,028 --> 00:03:58,696
It must have a key. I'll just look for it.

94
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:00,740
- We're going back?
- Just me.

95
00:04:00,823 --> 00:04:02,283
Wait here. Hide.

96
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:16,631
[henchman] Chiro.

97
00:04:17,632 --> 00:04:18,633
Chiro.

98
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:20,510
Where is Chiro?

99
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:22,136
He should be here already.

100
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:27,433
[tense music playing]

101
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,081
[music fades]

102
00:04:50,707 --> 00:04:52,458
Chiro! Chiro!

103
00:04:53,459 --> 00:04:54,669
Chiro!

104
00:04:56,254 --> 00:04:58,923
[tense music playing]

105
00:05:01,676 --> 00:05:04,304
[phone number pad beeping]

106
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:05,930
[line ringing]

107
00:05:06,764 --> 00:05:09,684
[in English] Sir Artem, we have a problem.

108
00:05:10,685 --> 00:05:13,813
[in English] This is a replica
of Casa Monroy,

109
00:05:13,896 --> 00:05:19,694
which is originally located
in Calle Arlegui, Quiapo, Manila.

110
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:24,324
[in English] The founder
of this heritage park believed that

111
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:29,162
the beauty of the Monroy family's home
was meant to be preserved.

112
00:05:29,245 --> 00:05:33,291
[in English] And so, he brought together
Filipino artisans

113
00:05:33,374 --> 00:05:39,047
to create a living tribute
to Filipino culture, craftsmanship,

114
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:40,673
and history.

115
00:05:41,382 --> 00:05:45,845
[in English] It's like restoring
and reimagining

116
00:05:45,928 --> 00:05:50,558
the magic of the original house.
It's brilliant.

117
00:05:51,225 --> 00:05:52,643
[in English] That's correct, madam.

118
00:05:53,436 --> 00:05:55,980
[Karla, in English] This house is filled
with so many intricate patterns,

119
00:05:56,064 --> 00:05:57,857
from the walls

120
00:05:57,940 --> 00:06:00,151
to the ceilings to the floors.

121
00:06:00,234 --> 00:06:02,737
[in English] Every single detail
has been carefully placed

122
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:06,616
by the founders of the heritage park.

123
00:06:06,699 --> 00:06:08,326
Please, Mr. Guard.

124
00:06:08,409 --> 00:06:10,828
Casa Monroy is the only one
we haven't entered.

125
00:06:11,579 --> 00:06:13,122
It's really prohibited, sir.

126
00:06:13,206 --> 00:06:14,373
We can't let anyone in anymore.

127
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:15,333
It's off-limits.

128
00:06:15,416 --> 00:06:16,709
Sorry.

129
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:17,794
What do you mean prohibited?

130
00:06:17,877 --> 00:06:19,921
I see foreigners

131
00:06:20,004 --> 00:06:22,673
posting on social media
that they're inside.

132
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:24,217
When it's foreigners, it's allowed?

133
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:25,760
When it's Filipinos, it's not?

134
00:06:26,344 --> 00:06:27,470
Come on, babe!

135
00:06:29,305 --> 00:06:30,139
Oh, no. What was that?

136
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:34,268
Wait. I thought
you were inside, Brother Kurt?

137
00:06:34,352 --> 00:06:37,772
Ah, I didn't join because Samir
seemed to recognize me.

138
00:06:38,481 --> 00:06:40,441
He might find out that I was the one

139
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:43,444
who pretended to be Sokolov
before, with Atoy.

140
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:45,154
At the Zahran embassy.

141
00:06:45,238 --> 00:06:46,531
- Sorry.
- It's okay, it's okay, it's okay.

142
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:48,241
Uno is inside anyway.

143
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:50,743
- [sighs]
- Brother Emerson!

144
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:52,120
[Emerson] Oh, Ibyang!

145
00:06:52,203 --> 00:06:53,913
[in English] Hey. Long time no see!

146
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:55,498
Wait a minute.

147
00:06:55,581 --> 00:06:56,415
What are you doing here?

148
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:58,501
Oh, hello to all of you!

149
00:06:58,584 --> 00:07:00,670
I missed you. Hmm.

150
00:07:01,379 --> 00:07:03,798
Uh, what's your mission?

151
00:07:04,674 --> 00:07:05,967
Is it inside?

152
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:07,844
Let me join!

153
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:10,388
Psst, hey. Did you tell her?

154
00:07:10,471 --> 00:07:13,182
Well, I just mentioned it,
but she's not coming.

155
00:07:13,266 --> 00:07:14,559
She's not in the plan.

156
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:17,061
Ibyang, stay here first, okay.

157
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:19,439
I'll go inside to perform, okay.

158
00:07:19,522 --> 00:07:20,648
Stay here.

159
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:22,900
Why did you tell her?

160
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:28,448
Uh, by the way, this is Sister Faye.

161
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:30,616
A friend of my Mama Olga.

162
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:33,744
Yes, a friend. I'm just her friend!

163
00:07:33,828 --> 00:07:36,497
[sobs]

164
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:37,582
[chuckles]

165
00:07:37,665 --> 00:07:38,958
Um, hi!

166
00:07:39,041 --> 00:07:42,170
[in English] My name is Charmielyn Faye!

167
00:07:42,253 --> 00:07:44,505
[Charmi] But you can be my friend.

168
00:07:44,589 --> 00:07:46,007
- [Charmi chuckles]
- Nice, huh.

169
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:48,092
She charmed you?

170
00:07:48,176 --> 00:07:49,135
Not me?

171
00:07:49,218 --> 00:07:50,887
[sneaky music playing]

172
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:53,431
You enchanted me!

173
00:07:54,557 --> 00:07:55,808
Oh, ah…

174
00:07:57,685 --> 00:07:58,519
[sneaky music playing]

175
00:07:58,603 --> 00:07:59,854
Wow. [titters]

176
00:07:59,937 --> 00:08:01,189
[in English] Coming from you?

177
00:08:01,272 --> 00:08:02,523
[both chuckling]

178
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:03,900
[Emerson, in English] Nice, huh.

179
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:05,485
- [chuckling]
- [Charmi] Yeah.

180
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:07,069
Do you always come here?

181
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:08,279
- [titters]
- [Kurt chuckles]

182
00:08:08,362 --> 00:08:11,115
[in English] What's your favorite drink,
your favorite color, you know?

183
00:08:11,199 --> 00:08:12,033
[in English] How many kids do you want?

184
00:08:12,116 --> 00:08:13,242
- [Kurt chuckles]
- [Charmi, in English] I want five.

185
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:14,577
[in English] Like a team, you know.

186
00:08:17,038 --> 00:08:18,539
[henchman] Is this
what you're looking for?

187
00:08:18,623 --> 00:08:20,458
- [keys jingling]
- [ominous music playing]

188
00:08:20,541 --> 00:08:21,375
‪[heavy breathing]

189
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:25,713
Hands up.

190
00:08:27,798 --> 00:08:29,675
[shouts] Hands up or I'll shoot you!

191
00:08:33,262 --> 00:08:34,597
Bro, take it easy.

192
00:08:36,557 --> 00:08:38,017
You can't kill me.

193
00:08:38,684 --> 00:08:40,645
I have what your boss is looking for.

194
00:08:41,604 --> 00:08:43,022
[henchman] You killed my companion.

195
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:45,691
I'll kill you too!

196
00:08:46,484 --> 00:08:49,278
[in English] Easy, easy.

197
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:52,281
We can talk this out.

198
00:08:53,866 --> 00:08:55,284
- [grunts]
- [gunshot]

199
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:59,121
[foreboding music playing]

200
00:09:00,122 --> 00:09:01,123
[gunshot]

201
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,002
[bone cracks]

202
00:09:07,838 --> 00:09:09,507
[thudding]

203
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:17,223
[in English] That is the point
of the founder.

204
00:09:17,306 --> 00:09:20,226
[in English] He wanted
to create this living heritage

205
00:09:20,309 --> 00:09:23,062
for the Filipinos who admire it
in the modern times.

206
00:09:23,145 --> 00:09:25,815
[in English] As you can tell,
this has been inspired

207
00:09:25,898 --> 00:09:28,734
by the Spanish colonial times.

208
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:32,697
[in English] From the beauty,
from the decor, from the furnishing,

209
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:35,199
from the art pieces that you can see.

210
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:38,077
[in English] From the red bricks,
flowers, ever-so-bright!

211
00:09:38,869 --> 00:09:40,037
[in English] Yes.

212
00:09:40,121 --> 00:09:41,664
[sneaky music playing]

213
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:48,754
[in English] This painting was painted
by one of the most

214
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:50,756
famous Filipino painters that we have.

215
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:53,259
[in English] As you can tell,
the art galleries that we have in Makati

216
00:09:53,342 --> 00:09:55,886
that recently has been

217
00:09:55,970 --> 00:10:00,391
actually thought of as an avocado
by one of our jurors.

218
00:10:00,474 --> 00:10:01,851
[in English] But no.
It's actually a coconut,

219
00:10:01,934 --> 00:10:03,936
and it's been one of the biggest supplies

220
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:06,147
that we have here in the Philippines.

221
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,734
I told you to stay with Emerson, right?

222
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:13,738
Eh, just let me join, Sister Ame.

223
00:10:13,821 --> 00:10:15,656
What exactly are we supposed to do?

224
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,118
Fine.

225
00:10:19,201 --> 00:10:23,623
What we need to do is get
Samir's cellphone or wallet, okay.

226
00:10:23,706 --> 00:10:24,874
What for?

227
00:10:24,957 --> 00:10:26,417
Stop asking too many questions.

228
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:27,710
Come on.

229
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,005
[Lily] Atoy.

230
00:10:31,088 --> 00:10:32,798
[music fades]

231
00:10:32,882 --> 00:10:35,343
- [tense music playing]
- [keys jingling]

232
00:10:35,426 --> 00:10:38,095
[Lily groans]

233
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:41,724
[Lily] It won't work.

234
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:44,727
I can't find it.

235
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:46,270
- There is one. All right.
- Ouch.

236
00:10:46,854 --> 00:10:48,356
Even that, the small one.
Try the small one.

237
00:10:48,439 --> 00:10:49,940
- [keys jingling]
- [Lily groaning]

238
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,484
- There.
- [Lily groans]

239
00:10:51,567 --> 00:10:53,569
- [keys jingling]
- [Lily sighs]

240
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:54,737
[panicked breathing]

241
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:58,783
[Karla, in English] If you guys have
any more questions about Casa Monroy,

242
00:10:58,866 --> 00:11:00,993
I am very much willing to answer.

243
00:11:01,077 --> 00:11:03,329
[music fades]

244
00:11:05,206 --> 00:11:08,793
[in English] Any other questions
about the family home?

245
00:11:08,876 --> 00:11:11,003
[in English] Do you like
any of these pieces, ma'am?

246
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:14,090
- [Anastacia, in English] Yes, lovely.
- [Karla, in English] Yeah.

247
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:15,716
[Anastacia, in English] It's the best.

248
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,218
[sneaky music playing]

249
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:20,471
Hey! You're rude!

250
00:11:20,554 --> 00:11:23,057
Why are you touching the woman, hmm?

251
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:26,936
Oop, oop, oop, oop!
Don't lie. I saw you. [scoffs]

252
00:11:27,019 --> 00:11:28,187
[in English] What?

253
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:30,064
[in English] What are you saying?

254
00:11:30,147 --> 00:11:31,273
Ah…

255
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:35,569
[Ibyang, in English] You do not touch
the back part of the woman.

256
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:37,655
[in English] The woman's back part,
especially this one.

257
00:11:37,738 --> 00:11:42,701
[in English] You do not touch that
without the…

258
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:43,661
consent, yes.

259
00:11:43,744 --> 00:11:45,663
[in English] You do not touch
the back part

260
00:11:45,746 --> 00:11:49,125
of the woman without their consent, yes.

261
00:11:49,208 --> 00:11:53,838
[in English] I learned that
in the… the school! Yes, the school.

262
00:11:53,921 --> 00:11:56,424
[in English] They call it…

263
00:11:56,507 --> 00:11:57,925
"chancing." Yes.

264
00:11:58,008 --> 00:12:00,136
[in English] You do not do the "chancing".

265
00:12:00,219 --> 00:12:03,180
[in English] Um, don't you have a teacher?

266
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:05,349
[Lily groans]

267
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:07,560
There. Did it go in?

268
00:12:07,643 --> 00:12:08,602
The other one, the other one.

269
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:09,562
[music fades]

270
00:12:09,645 --> 00:12:10,771
There, there, there.

271
00:12:11,814 --> 00:12:13,441
Quick, quick, quick, quick, quick.

272
00:12:13,524 --> 00:12:16,110
[Lily groans]

273
00:12:18,362 --> 00:12:19,572
What?

274
00:12:19,655 --> 00:12:21,073
[tense music playing]

275
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:22,283
[frustrated moaning]

276
00:12:22,366 --> 00:12:23,492
[sobs]

277
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:27,580
- There! [gasps] I found it.
- Yeah?

278
00:12:27,663 --> 00:12:29,957
[heavy breathing]

279
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:32,168
[gate hinge squeaking]

280
00:12:33,252 --> 00:12:36,005
- [tires screeching]
- [car door opens]

281
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:38,507
[music fades]

282
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:39,717
Where is Ivan?!

283
00:12:40,593 --> 00:12:43,095
[tense music playing]

284
00:12:43,179 --> 00:12:47,725
[in English] Did your parents not tell you
how to respect women?

285
00:12:48,559 --> 00:12:51,479
[in English] Are you sure
that he did that?

286
00:12:51,562 --> 00:12:53,606
[in English] Oh, mister.

287
00:12:53,689 --> 00:12:57,151
[in English] I am the very, very surest
of the very surest. Yes.

288
00:12:57,234 --> 00:12:59,612
[in English] I saw it with both my eyes.

289
00:12:59,695 --> 00:13:01,489
[in English] My one and the two eyes.

290
00:13:01,572 --> 00:13:04,033
[in English] Yes,
You know, my eyes? They're like, uh…

291
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:05,993
[in English] The eye--
They're like… eagle!

292
00:13:06,076 --> 00:13:08,245
[in English] You know the eagle?
The one that flies?

293
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:10,164
[in English] Yes. My eyes are like eagle.

294
00:13:10,247 --> 00:13:13,375
- [Ibyang, in English] I saw it.
- [in English] I'm so sorry, miss.

295
00:13:13,459 --> 00:13:14,919
[Anastacia, in English]
What are you doing?!

296
00:13:15,503 --> 00:13:17,129
[in English] I told you!

297
00:13:17,213 --> 00:13:19,924
[in English] You must be
on your best behavior!

298
00:13:20,007 --> 00:13:21,550
[in English] Why? Why are you like that?

299
00:13:22,134 --> 00:13:23,552
[Samir, in English] Okay.
Are we done here?

300
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:25,012
[in English] I have to go.
I have to go to work.

301
00:13:25,095 --> 00:13:26,472
[in English] Come on, let's go.

302
00:13:26,555 --> 00:13:30,059
[in English] Uh, would you like me
to call you a horse-drawn carriage?

303
00:13:30,142 --> 00:13:31,310
[in English] It can take you home.

304
00:13:31,393 --> 00:13:33,103
[in English] Of course, I like that.

305
00:13:34,104 --> 00:13:36,857
[in English] I like with horse.

306
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:37,900
- [in English] I really like--
- [Samir, in English] Mama likes a horse.

307
00:13:37,983 --> 00:13:39,193
- [in English] Come on, let's go.
- [in English] Yeah.

308
00:13:39,276 --> 00:13:40,861
[speaks in Russian] Hurry, hurry.

309
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:41,904
[in English] Come.

310
00:13:41,987 --> 00:13:44,448
[pensive music playing]

311
00:13:54,166 --> 00:13:56,252
[music fades]

312
00:13:57,711 --> 00:13:59,171
I said, where is Ivan?!

313
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:00,256
Who are you?!

314
00:14:01,465 --> 00:14:03,717
Ivan, uh… Uh…

315
00:14:04,218 --> 00:14:05,344
- [somber music playing]
- [grunts]

316
00:14:05,427 --> 00:14:06,762
Don't let the captives out!

317
00:14:08,847 --> 00:14:11,684
- [gunshots]
- [tense music playing]

318
00:14:12,268 --> 00:14:13,185
[shrieks]

319
00:14:19,692 --> 00:14:21,735
[Samir clears throat]

320
00:14:24,405 --> 00:14:26,532
[in English] Wait. Do you have my wallet?

321
00:14:26,615 --> 00:14:28,742
[suspicious music playing]

322
00:14:28,826 --> 00:14:31,620
[in English] I think I left it inside.
I'll be back.

323
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:36,166
[in English] So, where's the horse?

324
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:39,670
[in English] Uh, would you like to wait
a little longer or…

325
00:14:39,753 --> 00:14:42,756
[in English] No. Ma, let's go to the car.

326
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,675
[in English] Brother can wait
for us there.

327
00:14:46,677 --> 00:14:48,721
[in English] Thank you for the tour,

328
00:14:48,804 --> 00:14:52,600
and I'm sorry that happened with my son.

329
00:14:54,059 --> 00:14:56,687
[in English] I will tell Sir Samir
to follow, madam.

330
00:15:05,696 --> 00:15:07,323
[music fades]

331
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:09,909
[ominous music playing]

332
00:15:21,795 --> 00:15:23,005
[music fades]

333
00:15:25,132 --> 00:15:28,802
[suspicious music playing]

334
00:15:42,232 --> 00:15:46,820
[music swells]

335
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:22,982
[music fades]

336
00:16:23,065 --> 00:16:24,525
[ominous music playing]

337
00:16:27,111 --> 00:16:28,529
[in English] Looking for something?

338
00:16:28,612 --> 00:16:31,448
[in English] Yes. I, uh…
I dropped my wallet somewhere.

339
00:16:31,532 --> 00:16:32,658
[in English] I was here earlier.

340
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:34,284
[in English] A brown wallet…

341
00:16:35,452 --> 00:16:36,495
[in English] And what?

342
00:16:38,122 --> 00:16:40,958
- [in English] Maybe you can…
- [in English] Right… Right here.

343
00:16:45,629 --> 00:16:46,880
[tense music playing]

344
00:16:48,465 --> 00:16:50,759
I lied to you earlier, Samir.

345
00:16:51,927 --> 00:16:55,931
[in English] In fact,
I was a Sokolov brother.

346
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:57,016
[cackles]

347
00:16:57,099 --> 00:17:01,311
I was with Atoy pretending
at your embassy!

348
00:17:01,854 --> 00:17:03,647
[in English] Ah! Surprise!

349
00:17:03,731 --> 00:17:04,648
[in English] Yes.

350
00:17:04,732 --> 00:17:06,734
[speaks in Russian]
I knew it. You're an impostor.

351
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:09,778
[in English] I will kill you.

352
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:11,405
[grunts]

353
00:17:11,488 --> 00:17:13,157
[tense music playing]

354
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,450
[grunting]

355
00:17:16,827 --> 00:17:18,370
[in English] Let me go.

356
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:19,705
[in English] Where is my brother?!

357
00:17:19,788 --> 00:17:20,664
[in English] In hell!

358
00:17:20,748 --> 00:17:21,707
[in English] Would you like to say hello?

359
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:23,542
[grunting]

360
00:17:23,625 --> 00:17:24,793
[in English] You?

361
00:17:24,877 --> 00:17:26,545
[Samir, in English] Where do you think

362
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:29,089
you are going?

363
00:17:29,673 --> 00:17:33,385
[in English] The…
The ouchy… muscle, ouchy muscle!

364
00:17:33,469 --> 00:17:34,720
[in English] I know you!

365
00:17:34,803 --> 00:17:35,679
[in English] I know you too!

366
00:17:35,763 --> 00:17:37,264
[in English] You kidnapped Atoy!
Where did you put him?!

367
00:17:37,347 --> 00:17:38,390
- [gunshots]
- [Lily] Ouch!

368
00:17:38,474 --> 00:17:40,476
- [groans]
- [gunshots]

369
00:17:40,559 --> 00:17:42,478
- [tense music playing]
- [Lily groans]

370
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:43,687
[Lily] Atoy!

371
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:44,605
[Lily gasps]

372
00:17:46,523 --> 00:17:47,441
[music swells]

373
00:17:47,524 --> 00:17:49,193
[in English] You will pay for this.

374
00:17:49,276 --> 00:17:51,987
[Uno, in English] You are the real threat
to our national security!

375
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:54,198
[in English] Tell us where Atoy Padua is.

376
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:55,991
Answer if you don't want to get hurt!

377
00:17:57,701 --> 00:18:02,289
[grunting and groaning]

378
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:04,416
[Lily groans]

379
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:05,876
[Ivan] Don't kill him!

380
00:18:05,959 --> 00:18:06,794
We need him alive!

381
00:18:06,877 --> 00:18:10,631
[gunshots blasting]

382
00:18:12,424 --> 00:18:13,675
- Come on!
- [Lily] Atoy!

383
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:14,760
- Come on!
- [Lily] Let me go!

384
00:18:14,843 --> 00:18:16,970
Don't resist! I'll kill you!

385
00:18:17,054 --> 00:18:17,721
- [squeals]
- [gunshots]

386
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:21,809
[grunting and groaning]

387
00:18:21,892 --> 00:18:24,728
[grunting and growling]

388
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:25,771
- [grunting and growling]
- [music swells]

389
00:18:25,854 --> 00:18:26,688
Hold him, hold him!

390
00:18:27,314 --> 00:18:28,565
[grunting and growling]

391
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:29,733
[Kurt, in English] I got him!

392
00:18:29,817 --> 00:18:30,734
[grunting and growling]

393
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:33,487
[groaning]

394
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:36,156
What's wrong with you, Emerson?!

395
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:38,242
- [Emerson stammers]
- [Kurt] Why did you involve us?!

396
00:18:38,325 --> 00:18:39,493
[Emerson, in English] Collateral damage!

397
00:18:39,576 --> 00:18:40,911
[in English] Collateral damage! Sorry!

398
00:18:40,994 --> 00:18:42,871
[in English] Only pepper, no spray!

399
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:46,375
- [groaning]
- What just happened?

400
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:48,210
[gunshots]

401
00:18:48,293 --> 00:18:49,002
[shrieks]

402
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:49,962
- [thug] Let's go!
- [Lily] Ouch!

403
00:18:51,713 --> 00:18:53,090
[clamoring]

404
00:18:53,173 --> 00:18:54,216
[grunts]

405
00:18:54,299 --> 00:18:55,801
- [gunshots]
- [music fades]

406
00:18:57,344 --> 00:18:58,804
[Uno] Hurry, hurry!

407
00:18:58,887 --> 00:19:00,013
[Gavin] Oh no.

408
00:19:00,097 --> 00:19:02,641
[tense music playing]

409
00:19:20,284 --> 00:19:22,870
[pensive music playing]

410
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:28,375
Sorry. I also need your finger.

411
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:29,459
[phone blips]

412
00:19:29,543 --> 00:19:31,044
[Karla groans]

413
00:19:37,759 --> 00:19:38,844
[phone blips]

414
00:19:38,927 --> 00:19:40,888
[chuckles] Yes.

415
00:19:40,971 --> 00:19:42,222
I already sent it.

416
00:19:42,306 --> 00:19:44,683
Ah, good-- good job,
children of the thread.

417
00:19:44,766 --> 00:19:46,310
We really are the best!

418
00:19:46,393 --> 00:19:48,061
- [clears throat]
- Good job, really good job.

419
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:50,022
We're certified kidnappers now.

420
00:19:50,606 --> 00:19:51,857
That's enough.

421
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:53,025
Let's move on.

422
00:19:53,942 --> 00:19:55,027
[Uno] Let's go.

423
00:19:55,110 --> 00:19:56,195
[music fades]

424
00:19:56,778 --> 00:19:57,905
[grunts]

425
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:03,285
[Ivan, in English] Sir--

426
00:20:03,368 --> 00:20:04,578
[groans, gasps]

427
00:20:04,661 --> 00:20:05,871
[ominous music playing]

428
00:20:05,954 --> 00:20:07,039
[in English] Sir, I'm sorry.

429
00:20:07,122 --> 00:20:08,290
[in English] Idiot!

430
00:20:08,373 --> 00:20:10,417
[Ivan, in English]
We recaptured the prisoners.

431
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:12,836
[in English] They are back in their cell.

432
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:14,546
[in English] I'm sorry, sir.

433
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:17,132
[in English] As they should be, stupid!

434
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:21,553
[in English] You endangered
my good record for our boss!

435
00:20:21,637 --> 00:20:22,763
[tense music playing]

436
00:20:22,846 --> 00:20:24,306
[groans]

437
00:20:24,389 --> 00:20:26,308
- [in English] Consider yourself lucky,
- [coughs]

438
00:20:26,391 --> 00:20:28,227
because if the prisoners escape,

439
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:30,646
I myself will cut your throat.

440
00:20:30,729 --> 00:20:32,522
- [in English] Now, get out of my face!
- [grunts]

441
00:20:36,443 --> 00:20:38,987
[in English] Reinforce perimeter.
Immediately!

442
00:20:39,863 --> 00:20:41,240
[music swells]

443
00:20:47,162 --> 00:20:48,872
What's wrong with you, Ibyang?

444
00:20:48,956 --> 00:20:50,749
Why did you run away from me earlier?

445
00:20:50,832 --> 00:20:54,086
What if something happened to you, huh?

446
00:20:54,169 --> 00:20:55,587
If something bad happened to you,

447
00:20:55,671 --> 00:20:59,174
Mama Olga would have been angry at me!

448
00:21:02,010 --> 00:21:04,805
Nothing bad happened.

449
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:08,350
What I did was effective.

450
00:21:08,433 --> 00:21:11,144
I even helped. Right, Sister Ame?

451
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:15,148
That's not the point, Ibyang.

452
00:21:15,232 --> 00:21:17,609
You really can't stay put.

453
00:21:17,693 --> 00:21:20,404
Do I always have to remind you?

454
00:21:25,325 --> 00:21:26,243
[phone blips]

455
00:21:26,326 --> 00:21:27,786
Oh. There, Ibyang.

456
00:21:27,869 --> 00:21:29,454
Your Mama Olga texted.

457
00:21:29,538 --> 00:21:30,998
She's on her way.

458
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:34,126
[Charmi] Psst, Ibyang.

459
00:21:35,085 --> 00:21:36,503
Just stay quiet about what happened, okay.

460
00:21:36,586 --> 00:21:38,213
Don't spill it to your mama.

461
00:21:40,757 --> 00:21:41,883
Mmm.

462
00:21:42,759 --> 00:21:44,136
Be careful there, okay.

463
00:21:44,219 --> 00:21:45,637
Behave.

464
00:21:48,056 --> 00:21:52,269
Sister Ame, mmm, do you still see

465
00:21:52,853 --> 00:21:54,146
Mama Mary?

466
00:21:54,229 --> 00:21:55,981
Mama Mary? Who?

467
00:21:56,064 --> 00:21:58,692
Ah, she's referring to her Aunt Audrey,

468
00:21:58,775 --> 00:22:00,652
whom she calls Mama Mary.

469
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:03,113
Of course. Why do you ask?

470
00:22:05,198 --> 00:22:06,783
Because…

471
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:09,453
[gentle music playing]

472
00:22:10,579 --> 00:22:12,497
[Ibyang] Please give this to her.

473
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:17,961
Because I always think of her

474
00:22:18,045 --> 00:22:19,963
whenever I see porridge.

475
00:22:23,175 --> 00:22:24,801
I'll give this to her.

476
00:22:26,219 --> 00:22:28,055
Thank you, Sister Ame.

477
00:22:28,138 --> 00:22:30,724
Welcome. Take care, okay.

478
00:22:32,392 --> 00:22:35,395
[sentimental music playing]

479
00:22:49,993 --> 00:22:51,411
[music fades]

480
00:22:56,708 --> 00:23:00,212
[somber music playing]

481
00:23:01,213 --> 00:23:02,923
[phone ringing]

482
00:23:05,801 --> 00:23:07,177
[Emerson] I'll answer.

483
00:23:07,260 --> 00:23:09,304
[phone ringing]

484
00:23:10,639 --> 00:23:11,890
Hello?

485
00:23:13,767 --> 00:23:14,810
[Artem, in English] <i>Who are you?</i>

486
00:23:15,602 --> 00:23:17,562
[in English] <i>Why do you have</i>
<i>Samir's phone?</i>

487
00:23:21,900 --> 00:23:24,069
[in English] I'm the one
who captured Samir.

488
00:23:24,152 --> 00:23:25,278
[in English] We have him.

489
00:23:26,696 --> 00:23:28,490
[Artem, in English]
<i>What did you do to him?</i>

490
00:23:29,533 --> 00:23:30,700
[heavy music playing]

491
00:23:31,284 --> 00:23:32,244
[in English] Nothing.

492
00:23:32,327 --> 00:23:34,162
[in English] He's just sleeping,
like Sleeping Beauty.

493
00:23:35,288 --> 00:23:36,498
[Artem, in English] <i>What do you want?</i>

494
00:23:37,082 --> 00:23:38,250
[in English] Listen.

495
00:23:39,042 --> 00:23:40,460
We'll exchange.

496
00:23:40,544 --> 00:23:41,628
[in English] Exchange heads.

497
00:23:42,796 --> 00:23:45,674
[in English] We give you Samir,
and you give us Atoy.

498
00:23:46,174 --> 00:23:47,134
[Artem smirks]

499
00:23:48,510 --> 00:23:50,470
[Artem, in English]
<i>I don't care if you kill Samir.</i>

500
00:23:51,179 --> 00:23:52,681
[in English] <i>You can do everything</i>
<i>you want to him.</i>

501
00:23:52,764 --> 00:23:54,307
[in English] <i>But your Atoy…</i>

502
00:23:54,391 --> 00:23:55,976
[Artem smirks]

503
00:23:56,059 --> 00:23:58,103
<i>…remains our prisoner.</i>

504
00:23:58,186 --> 00:23:59,437
[Artem cackles]

505
00:23:59,521 --> 00:24:00,856
- [line blips]
- [in English] Hello?

506
00:24:00,939 --> 00:24:02,274
[in English] Hello!

507
00:24:02,357 --> 00:24:04,484
[music fades]

508
00:24:07,654 --> 00:24:09,698
So, there's someone
even more demonic than him.

509
00:24:10,699 --> 00:24:12,742
They're willing to sacrifice Samir,

510
00:24:12,826 --> 00:24:14,703
but they won't return Atoy.

511
00:24:15,495 --> 00:24:17,455
So, what do we do now, huh?

512
00:24:17,539 --> 00:24:19,916
It looks like we're at a dead end.

513
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:21,251
[somber music playing]

514
00:24:22,669 --> 00:24:23,795
No.

515
00:24:24,838 --> 00:24:27,174
No, no. There's another way.

516
00:24:28,842 --> 00:24:32,512
I'll call our boss to consult him.

517
00:24:32,596 --> 00:24:36,224
[heavy music playing]

518
00:24:41,271 --> 00:24:44,274
Alcaraz, we were sent by Major Mercado.

519
00:24:44,357 --> 00:24:46,067
We'll take care of him.

520
00:24:47,152 --> 00:24:48,612
Thank you very much, Santos.

521
00:24:48,695 --> 00:24:50,572
[Santos, in English]
We will detain him for interrogation.

522
00:24:50,655 --> 00:24:53,283
Then we will strike a deal
with the Zahran ambassador,

523
00:24:53,366 --> 00:24:54,910
so we can get Padua.

524
00:24:56,203 --> 00:24:57,120
[Uno, in English] All right.

525
00:24:57,204 --> 00:24:58,205
Let's go.

526
00:24:58,830 --> 00:25:00,248
You take care of him.

527
00:25:01,082 --> 00:25:01,917
[in English] Let's go.

528
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:05,378
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

529
00:25:07,339 --> 00:25:09,090
[Santos] I just need to make a call.

530
00:25:21,394 --> 00:25:23,104
[music fades]

531
00:25:28,109 --> 00:25:31,029
[tense music playing]

532
00:25:38,703 --> 00:25:40,413
[electronic blipping]

533
00:25:41,873 --> 00:25:46,795
- [music intensifies]
- [electronic blipping]

534
00:25:49,589 --> 00:25:52,717
There are three people here, collecting.

535
00:25:52,801 --> 00:25:54,469
Those three men you talked to,

536
00:25:54,552 --> 00:25:55,595
they're enemies!

537
00:25:55,679 --> 00:25:57,555
No, they're gone. They already left!

538
00:25:58,765 --> 00:25:59,933
They're actually there!

539
00:26:00,016 --> 00:26:01,434
There, look!

540
00:26:01,518 --> 00:26:03,853
‪UP NEXT

541
00:26:03,937 --> 00:26:05,105
[henchman 1] Nothing.

542
00:26:05,188 --> 00:26:07,357
Where is Audrey going? To Atoy, of course.

543
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:09,276
Send people to Tabang Lupa.

544
00:26:09,359 --> 00:26:10,485
Let them do surveillance there.

545
00:26:10,568 --> 00:26:13,029
[Martina] If you see them,
don't ever hurt my son.

546
00:26:13,655 --> 00:26:17,158
And make sure you bring Audrey
and Janine here immediately. Okay?

547
00:26:17,742 --> 00:26:18,618
[in English] What did you do to them?

548
00:26:18,702 --> 00:26:20,912
[in English] So now that I have

549
00:26:22,289 --> 00:26:25,625
your Audrey and your precious daughter…

550
00:26:27,877 --> 00:26:31,798
who will protect them from men like me?

551
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:34,009
[in English] I'll tell you where it is.

552
00:26:35,093 --> 00:26:37,220
[in English] I will tell you
where the laptop is.

553
00:26:37,304 --> 00:26:38,847
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

554
00:26:38,930 --> 00:26:41,016
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

555
00:26:41,099 --> 00:26:44,352
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

556
00:26:44,436 --> 00:26:46,521
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

557
00:26:46,604 --> 00:26:47,939
‪Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
